+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""The tree checks -- the library diffed against the documents that describe it (`meta/specs/TESTING.md` §5,
+@@PD-175@@). What a specification states as data each reads FROM the specification, never from a copy of it here --
+B-18's table, §3's identities, K-1's calls, every stated kernel constant and structure size, the rules a citation
+names -- and where its rule is a sentence it states that rule's words: S-1's `MSG_NOSIGNAL`, S-2's `write` and
+`ByteWriter`, V-3's port, P-1's file. It reads `.npk` source only through `lexical.py`, as bytes: the code with every
+comment and literal blanked, and a comment's words only where the check reads them -- a module's header line, a
+citation. And it prints what it examined, so a check whose input is empty today says so rather than passing in
+silence. Every one fails the run on a finding, `check_specs_current`
+included (the planning guide's G20). Each returns `(line, findings)`; the run prints the line, and each finding as a
+`FAIL` line of its own.
+
+  check_layering           every `use` between modules under `src/`, read where the code holds it, against the
+                           importer's row of `BUILD.md` B-18's table; each module's `// MAY IMPORT:` header line
+                           against its row; and no cycle among the files' imports (B-19)
+  check_error_budget       every `error:` declared under `src/` a name of `SAFETY.md` §3's table, declared once, in
+                           the directory its row names; and every identity a `fail` site raises, keyed by (module,
+                           name) and private ones included, one the table declares (S-4, S-8; the early ecosystem
+                           audit's EC3) -- a name declared by a second module is a second identity every consumer owes
+  check_constants_named    every `sys` call under `src/` names its number by a `SYS_<CALL>` constant `src/sys/`
+                           declares, its call one of `SOCKET_MODEL.md` K-1's table, its value K-1's; no `SYS_` name and
+                           no kernel constant a specification states -- `NAME` = n or `NAME` (n), a bound's `NSOCK_`
+                           aside -- declared outside `src/sys/`, and each declared there at the value stated; and no
+                           `NSOCK_` bound declared outside `src/core/limits.npk`, nor a value that file declares
+                           written as a literal elsewhere under `src/`
+  check_no_hardcoded_port  no non-zero integer literal bound or initialised to a name whose word is `port` --
+                           `port`, `port_be`, `sin_port` -- in `tests/` (V-3)
+  check_msg_nosignal       every `sys` call under `src/` whose number is `sendto`'s or `sendmsg`'s by K-1's table names
+                           `MSG_NOSIGNAL` in its flags argument (S-1, V-11)
